            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Dedication to Science and Education</strong><br>\nGolgi was dedicated to scientific research and teaching, inspiring future generations of scientists through his work at the University of Pavia.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy in Medical Science</strong><br>\nThe legacy of Camillo Golgi includes the Golgi tendon organ, which he discovered, and his contributions to the understanding of cellular processes and neuroscience.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Continuing Influence</strong><br>\nGolgi passed away on January 21, 1926. His work continues to be a cornerstone of cellular biology and neuroscience, influencing contemporary research and education.</p>\n"
              },
